#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:3
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:5
msgid ""
"For benchmarking a patch we want to reduce all possible sources of noise as "
"much as possible. How to do that is very OS dependent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:8
msgid ""
"Note that low noise is required, but not sufficient. It does not exclude "
"measurement bias. See [\"Producing Wrong Data Without Doing Anything "
"Obviously Wrong!\" by Mytkowicz, Diwan, Hauswith and Sweeney (ASPLOS 2009)]"
"(https://users.cs.northwestern.edu/~robby/courses/322-2013-spring/mytkowicz-"
"wrong-data.pdf) for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:13
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:15
msgid "Use a high-resolution timer, e.g., perf under Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:17
msgid "Run the benchmark multiple times to be able to recognize noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:19
msgid "Disable as many processes or services as possible on the target system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:21
msgid ""
"Disable frequency scaling, Turbo Boost and address space randomization (see "
"OS-specific section)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:24
msgid ""
"Use static linking if the OS supports it. That avoids any variation that "
"might be introduced by loading dynamic libraries. This can be done by "
"passing `-DLLVM_BUILD_STATIC=ON` to CMake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Benchmarking.md:28
msgid ""
"Try to avoid storage. On some systems, you can use tmpfs. Putting the "
"program, inputs and outputs on tmpfs avoids touching a real storage system, "
"which can have a pretty big variability."
msgstr ""

